\DOC REPEAT_GEN_AND_OFFSET_STACKPTR_TAC

\TYPE {REPEAT_GEN_AND_OFFSET_STACKPTR_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Strips all leading universal quantifiers from the goal's conclusion, fixing the
bound variables as free variables.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal whose conclusion is {!x1 ... xn. t}, it
repeatedly generalizes, leaving the body {t} as the conclusion with {x1 ... xn}
now free variables of the goal; nothing else in the conclusion changes.
{
   ?- !x1 ... xn. t
   ================  REPEAT_GEN_AND_OFFSET_STACKPTR_TAC
   ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces this is the only transformation seen, always yielding
exactly one subgoal, and only on goals with no assumptions whose conclusions
are universally quantified implications about machine-code {ensures}
statements.

\ENDDOC
